abstract: >
  Telemachus is an open, Parquet-native format for high-frequency telematics
  data (GNSS+IMU). The specification defines 25 columns across 7 functional
  groups, 3 device profiles (core/imu/full), and a dataset manifest (SPEC-02).
  Version 1.0 adds format adapters that convert data the project has never seen
  — CSV through a declarative column-and-unit mapping, GPX and NMEA 0183 —
  alongside the dataset adapters for AEGIS, PVS and STRIDE. It makes the
  manifest row accounting normative, so a consumer can audit what an adapter
  discarded; adds unit plausibility checking, which catches the wrong-unit
  defect every schema check passes; and introduces carrier profiles, opening
  the manifest to carriers that are not vehicles without changing what a
  vehicle means.
